{"availability":"available","full":"wieslawsoltes/Win95","name":"Win95","description":"Windows 95 desktop recreated in the browser with JavaScript ES modules, HTML and CSS — window management, a shared virtual filesystem, document and drawing tools, games and a DOS-style command interpreter.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":6,"forks":1,"created":"2026-10-04T16:46:49Z","updated":"2026-10-04T16:55:30Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://wieslawsoltes.github.io/Win95/","topics":["browser-os","desktop-environment","es-modules","github-pages","javascript","retro","web-desktop","webgpu","win95","windows","windows-95"],"demo":"https://wieslawsoltes.github.io/Win95/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:05.359Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:05.359Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:05.359Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:04:05.359Z","stars":6,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Live demo: — The Deploy to GitHub Pages workflow publishes the build-free desktop in public/os/ on every push to main.","A browser-native recreation of the Windows 95 desktop, with working window management, a shared virtual filesystem, document and drawing tools, games, and a DOS-style command interpreter. The desktop is written in JavaScript ES modules, HTML, and CSS. Six packages separate its storage, controls, shell, rendering, applications, and game rules.","This project recreates familiar interactions and visual details. It does not include the Windows kernel or execute native Windows or DOS binaries, and visual equivalence has not been established by exhaustive screenshot comparison. See compatibility and limitations for the precise scope."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/Win95/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7842b84d1dd1e00c1ec3593ac6d0afa5d6d541df75953ecc5f5e1a529b9e5dcc","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:05.440Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04: